Generated with pymavlink 2.4.49 (mavgen.py, bundled C generator), from
common/mavlink/mabur.xml (which includes common/mavlink/common.xml,
minimal.xml and standard.xml -- copied from the same pymavlink package's
message_definitions/v1.0/).

Regenerate with:
  nix-shell -p python3Packages.pymavlink --run "mavgen.py --lang C --wire-protocol 2.0 -o third_party/mavlink common/mavlink/mabur.xml"

protocol.h is hand-patched after generation: mav_array_assign_char and
_mav_put_char_array copy with mav_array_memcpy, not the generator's
strncpy, because mabur's PARAM_EXT_SET/VALUE/ACK carry raw bytes in a
char[] field, not a NUL-terminated string. Reapply that patch after
regenerating.

The MABUR_CAL_KIND_FLOOR and MABUR_CAL_ACK_RESULT_NO_PAIR entries in
mabur/mabur.h were added by hand from mabur.xml (enum entries only: no
message layout or CRC_EXTRA changed); a regenerate with the pinned
pymavlink reproduces them.
